course: dictionary
lesson: 10218
title: The many meanings of title
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A title is the name given to something, like a book, film, song or picture. It usually sits at the top, so you read it first. «A headline is the title of a news story; it is short, bold and grabs attention.» The headline is the news story's name.
explain: Title has more than one meaning, so use the context to choose. Ask yourself: is this about a name, a rank, a sports prize or a legal right? «Pharaoh, the title of the kings of ancient Egypt» shows a title can be a rank. Pharaoh was the name given to their kings.
explain: Titles like Mr, Mrs, Ms, Dr, Sir and Lady come before a person's name to show who they are. Words like shūshu (uncle) and āyí (auntie) also tell you how someone is related to you or how you should treat them.
explain: As a verb, to title means to give a name to a book, song or piece of work. When you title your story, you choose the name for it.
fact: A title is the name of a book, film, song, picture or piece of writing.
fact: A title can be a word used before a person's name, such as Mr, Mrs, Ms, Dr, Sir or Lady.
fact: In sport, a title is the position of champion, as in «She won the world title.»
fact: «Pharaoh» is the title of the kings of ancient Egypt.
fact: As a verb, to title means to give a name to a book, song or work.
exercise: «She won the world title in swimming.» What does title mean here? | A word before a person's name | A name for a book | *The position of champion in sport | The right to own a piece of land
exercise: «Pharaoh, the title of the kings of ancient Egypt» What does title mean in this sentence? | A picture of a king | A song about Egypt | *A rank or name given to the kings
exercise: Mia says title only means the name of a book. Which word is a title before a person's name? | Table | Ladder | *Dr | Garden
test: What does it mean to title a song? | To delete it | To sing it loudly | *To give it a name | To hide it away
test: Why does a bar chart need a title? | To show how old the chart is | To make the page look pretty | To decorate the page | *To tell what the data show
exam: Which is NOT a meaning of title? | The champion in a sport | *A type of fruit | The name of a book or film | A word before a name, like Mr
